## Phase Details

### Phase 1: Discovery & Planning

**Objectives**:
- Understand clinical workflows and requirements
- Define success metrics
- Establish governance and team

**Activities**:

| Activity | Duration | Participants |
|----------|----------|--------------|
| Kickoff Meeting | 2 hours | All stakeholders |
| Current State Assessment | 2-3 days | Clinical, IT |
| Requirements Workshop | 1 day | Clinical leads |
| Integration Planning | 1 day | IT, MedSync |
| Project Plan Finalization | 1 day | PM, Customer |

**Deliverables**:
- Project charter
- Requirements document
- Integration plan
- Detailed project schedule
- RACI matrix

### Phase 2: Configuration

**Objectives**:
- Configure MedSync to match workflows
- Set up organizational structure
- Build integrations

**Activities**:

| Activity | Duration | Owner |
|----------|----------|-------|
| Org Structure Setup | 1-2 days | MedSync |
| User Role Configuration | 1-2 days | Joint |
| Workflow Configuration | 3-5 days | Joint |
| Care Plan Templates | 2-3 days | Clinical |
| Alert Configuration | 1-2 days | Clinical |
| Integration Development | 2-4 weeks | MedSync + IT |

**Deliverables**:
- Configured environment
- Workflow documentation
- Integration specifications

### Phase 3: Data & Integration

**Objectives**:
- Complete EHR integration
- Migrate historical data (if applicable)
- Validate data quality

**Activities**:

| Activity | Duration | Owner |
|----------|----------|-------|
| EHR Connection | 1-2 weeks | MedSync + Vendor |
| Data Mapping | 1 week | Joint |
| Historical Migration | 1-2 weeks | MedSync |
| Data Validation | 1 week | Joint |
| Integration Testing | 1 week | Joint |

**Integration Options**:

| Method | Timeline | Best For |
|--------|----------|----------|
| FHIR R4 | 2-3 weeks | Modern EHRs |
| HL7 v2 | 3-4 weeks | Legacy systems |
| API | 2-3 weeks | Custom systems |
| File/Batch | 1-2 weeks | Limited integration |

### Phase 4: Testing

**Objectives**:
- Validate functionality
- Ensure integration reliability
- Verify security and performance

**Test Types**:

| Test Type | Duration | Participants |
|-----------|----------|--------------|
| Integration Testing | 1 week | IT, MedSync |
| Functional Testing | 1 week | Super-users |
| User Acceptance Testing | 1-2 weeks | End-users |
| Performance Testing | 2-3 days | MedSync |
| Security Testing | 2-3 days | Security, MedSync |

**Exit Criteria**:
- All critical defects resolved
- UAT sign-off from stakeholders
- Integration success rate >99%
- Performance within SLAs

### Phase 5: Training

**Objectives**:
- Enable end-user adoption
- Build internal expertise
- Prepare support processes

**Training Approach**:

| Role | Training Type | Duration |
|------|---------------|----------|
| Super Users | Train-the-Trainer | 8 hours |
| End Users | Role-based | 2-4 hours |
| Administrators | Admin training | 4 hours |
| IT Support | Technical training | 4 hours |

**Training Modalities**:
- Live virtual instructor-led
- On-site classroom (optional)
- Self-paced eLearning
- Quick reference guides
- Video library

### Phase 6: Go-Live

**Objectives**:
- Successful production launch
- Minimize disruption
- Rapid issue resolution

**Go-Live Approach**:

| Approach | Description | Recommended For |
|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| Big Bang | All users at once | <100 users |
| Phased | By department/location | 100-500 users |
| Pilot + Rollout | Pilot group first | >500 users |

**Hypercare**:

| Week | Support Level | MedSync Presence |
|------|---------------|------------------|
| Week 1 | 24/7 on-call | On-site (optional) |
| Week 2 | Extended hours | Virtual |
| Week 3-4 | Standard + priority | Virtual |
| Week 5+ | Standard support | Standard |

